Generate {{ num_docs }} realistic English business email excerpts following these rules.

## Rules
- Each email must be independent with different senders, recipients, and content
- Mark PII entities with the following XML tags:
  - <PERSON>full name</PERSON>
  - <ADDRESS>full mailing address</ADDRESS>
  - <ORGANIZATION>company or institution name</ORGANIZATION>
  - <DATE_OF_BIRTH>date of birth</DATE_OF_BIRTH> (only when applicable)
  - <BANK_ACCOUNT>bank account information (bank name, routing number, account number, account type)</BANK_ACCOUNT> (only when applicable)
- Text outside tags must be natural English prose
- Write in formal business email style
- Mix name formats: first-last, with middle initials, with titles (Mr./Ms./Dr.), hyphenated names (O'Brien, Jean-Pierre), suffixes (Jr., III)
- Addresses: include street number, street name, city, state, zip code; vary with suite/apt/floor; include US, UK, Canadian formats
- Date of birth formats MUST vary across these: "January 15, 1990", "01/15/1990", "15 Jan 1990", "1990-01-15", "15-Jan-1990", "DOB: MM/DD/YYYY"
- Bank account info MUST include bank name + routing number + account number + account type (e.g., "Chase Bank, Routing: 021000021, Account: 123456789, Checking")
- Each email should be 100-300 words

## Output format
Separate each email with `---DOC_SEPARATOR---`

## Topic examples
- Invoice submission to a client, new customer registration confirmation, bank account change notification, follow-up after a business meeting, employee transfer announcement